<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reginar IV, Count of Mons</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 950–1013</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reginar IV was a son of the exiled Reginar III who fought for decades to recover his family's lands in Hainaut. Helped by his marriage to Hedwig, daughter of the French king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-capet">Hugh Capet</a>, he regained the county of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mons">Mons</a> by the end of the tenth century, restoring the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reginarids">Reginarids</a>, whose lines later ruled Hainaut and Brabant.</p></div>
